    "body": "> This doesn't work when resource is a session history entry, which I'm pretty sure is a thing it can be.\r\n\r\nWhen _resource_ is a session history entry, no substep in \r\n\r\n> 12. This is the step that attempts to obtain resource, if necessary. Jump to the first appropriate substep:\r\n\r\nworks, so I think that's out-of-scope? Or are you asking me to fix the existing spec first?",
